ts.", "watch": "A late shift toward Sununu on cost-of-living issues, amplified by heavy Republican outside spending, could narrow the polling lead.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Jeanne Shaheen (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Hampshire's Senate seat is open with Jeanne Shaheen retiring, and Representative Chris Pappas faces former Senator John Sununu. Polling through late October consistently shows Pappas ahead, with margins of five to eight points across pollsters of varied affiliations, including Republican-linked firms. The state's slight Democratic lean and a national climate that has favored Democrats this cycle underpin his advantage.\n\nPappas has heavily out-raised Sununu, though outside groups have spent more to boost Sununu than to support Pappas. Expert raters split between Lean D and Likely D, and prediction markets price Pappas's chances around ninety percent. Sununu's family name keeps Republicans competitive in a state they have won statewide before, but the polling consensus and financial edge point to Pappas as the clear favorite heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8721, "margin": 5.76}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8221, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7959, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8661, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8028, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.837, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8746, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8609, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.856, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8659, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8474, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8665, "margin": 5.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.841, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8206, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_